---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_452",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 452,
  "text": "[[2017.4]] <b>367₅.  De causa motus DE CAUSA MOTUS </p>\n<p> [[2017.5]] <b>Punctum moveri</b> dicitur quod distantiam ab aliis punctis mutat ob causam in\n[[2017.6]] ipso existentem. </p>\n<p> [[2017.7]] <b>Duorum punctorum <i>A</b> <b>et <i>B</b> <b>motus communis</b> est si quatenus ita moventur\n[[2017.8]] eandem distantiam servent; ut liquidum cum vase, etsi per accidens eveniat, ut partes\n[[2017.9]] liquidi ob vas nonnihil concussum separatum aliquem motum accipiant. Si vero corpus\n[[2017.10]] esset firmum partes ejus absolute distantiam eandem servarent. </p>\n<p> [[2017.11]] <b>Corpus moveri</b> dicitur, si nulla ejus pars sit in qua non punctum assumi possit,\n[[2017.12]] quod communi cum caeteris motu moveatur. Hinc patet cur dicatur corpus moveri circa\n[[2017.13]] suum axem, etsi puncta ejus aliqua nempe in axe motus sita, quiescant. Chorda vero quae\n[[2017.14]] ab utroque extremo extenditur, non ideo moveri dicitur, nam motus nullus est per se\n[[2017.15]] partibus (si totum ut firmum consideraretur) futurus communis, cum alia huc alia illuc\n[[2017.16]] magis trahantur. </p>\n<p> [[2017.17]] <b>Motus simplex</b> est cum omnia puncta moti describunt lineas parallelas, rectas\n[[2017.18]] scilicet vel peripherias. </p>\n<p> [[2017.19]] Porro ad motum desidero, non\n[[2017.20]] tantum mutationem situs ab aliis, sed\n[[2017.21]] etiam ut causa sit in eo cui motus\n[[2017.22]] ascribitur, nam si solam mutationem\n[[2017.23]] situs consideremus, seu quod in\n[[2017.24]] motu mere mathematicum est, non\n[[2017.25]] potest dici cuinam ex pluribus corporibus situm inter se variantibus motus sit ascriben\n[[2018.1]] dus. Unde fit etiam ut in Astronomicis tam multas hypotheses fingere liceat, qualis illa est\n[[2018.2]] nullo modo probabilis, quae lunam in centro mundi ponit; sed si ad causas physicas\n[[2018.3]] veniamus, facilius constat cuinam ascribendus sit motus. Exempli causa sint tria corpora\n[[2018.4]] <i>a, b, c</i> dicamque moveri corpus <i>c</i> in recta <i>1c2c</i>, poterit alius mihi contradicere et asserere\n[[2018.5]] non moveri ipsum <i>c</i>, sed quiescere, et ipsa <i>a, b</i> simul sumta potius contrario motu moveri\n[[2018.6]] ex <i>1b1a</i> in <i>2b2a</i> quae licet non aeque sit probabile, (simplicius enim est motum unius\n[[2018.7]] supponere quam duorum) est tamen possibile, nam situs primus ponatur esse <i>1a1b1c</i>\n[[2018.8]] translato <i>1c</i> in <i>2c</i> ipsis <i>1a</i> et <i>1b</i> manentibus tunc phaenomenon, quod orietur, erit situs\n[[2018.9]] <i>1a1b2c</i>; at ipso <i>1c</i> manente et <i>1a1b</i> translatis in <i>2a2b</i> tunc phaenomenon quod orietur,\n[[2018.10]] erit situs <i>2a2b1c</i> qui a priori phaenomeno seu situ <i>1a1b2c</i> non potest discerni, itaque nec\n[[2018.11]] judicari hinc potest, utra hypothesis sit vera. Idem est etsi quatuor corpora loco trium\n[[2018.12]] supponantur, tunc eadem phaenomena poterunt explicari per hypotheses adhuc multo\n[[2018.13]] plures. Nisi assumatur aliquod corpus novum <i>d</i> tale, ut corpus unum <i>c</i> si moveri ponatur\n[[2018.14]] ex <i>1c</i> in <i>2c</i>, in ipsum <i>d</i> impingere\n[[2018.15]] necesse sit, tunc enim a simplici\n[[2018.16]] consideratione mathematica situs\n[[2018.17]] variati, transitur ad physicam nempe\n[[2018.18]] ad aliquam actionem, sequetur enim\n[[2018.19]] aliqua motus communicatio, ex qua\n[[2018.20]] manifestum erit, actionem aliquam\n[[2018.21]] ipsi <i>c</i> esse ascribendam. </p>\n<p> [[2018.22]] <b>Locus</b> est situs qui distantia a\n[[2018.23]] punctis fixis in mundo sumtis determinatur. </p>\n<p> [[2018.25]] Hinc fieri potest, ut corpus sit in\n[[2018.26]] motu, seu vim quandam agendi habeat, locum tamen respectu punctorum immotorum\n[[2018.27]] circumjacentium non mutet. Exempli causa <i>e</i> moveatur in linea <i>fg</i> ab <i>f</i> versus <i>g</i>, et eodem\n[[2018.28]] tempore eadem celeritate tota linea <i>fg</i> contrario motu, sic ut vestigia lineae in ipsam\n[[2019.1]] lineam incidant, tendat ex <i>1f1g</i> in <i>2f2g</i>, ut si <i>e</i> sit homo, <i>fg</i> navis in qua homo spatietur a\n[[2019.2]] prora ad puppim, dum navis aequali celeritate progrediatur, manifestum est quo tempore\n[[2019.3]] <i>e</i> perveniet ab <i>f</i> in <i>g</i>, eodem tempore <i>1g</i> pervenire in <i>2g</i>, et quia ob aequalem celeritatem\n[[2019.4]] utriusque motus linea <i>fg</i> decursa ab <i>e</i> aequalis est lineae <i>1g2g</i> decursae a puncto <i>g</i>, ideo\n[[2019.5]] punctum <i>2g</i> incidet in punctum <i>1f</i>, et ideo <i>e</i>, quod sub finem motus pervenit in <i>g</i>, adeoque\n[[2019.6]] nunc est in <i>2g</i>, reperietur esse in <i>1f</i> ubi antea fuerat. Et idem semper et ubique durante hoc\n[[2019.7]] motu continget, adeoque <i>e</i> spectatum ex immotis <i>l, m, n</i> ne quidem progredi videbitur.\n[[2019.8]] Dicendum tamen est ipsum esse in motu; nam homo ille utique sentiet se spatiando\n[[2019.9]] fatigari, et motu suo pellere aliquid vel trahere poterit; ac proinde agit. Quoniam ergo\n[[2019.10]] motum ei tribuimus in quo causa mutati situs est, seu quod agit, utique corpus <i>e</i> moveri\n[[2019.11]] dicemus, etsi locum quem in mundo habet, et qui respectu punctorum fixorum sumendus\n[[2019.12]] est non mutet. Etsi autem nullum fortasse sit corpus fixum in mundo, tamen puncta fixa\n[[2019.13]] intellectu designari possunt, cognito enim motu, quo corpora ab suis locis digrediantur,\n[[2019.14]] constat etiam distantia locorum priorum a locis posterioribus. </p>\n<p> [[2019.15]] Qui motum corporis definiverunt translatione ex vicinia corporum immediate\n[[2019.16]] contingentium, et quae tanquam quiescentia spectantur in viciniam aliorum, illi non\n[[2019.17]] tantum commisere circulum in definiendo: nam quamdiu non intelligitur, quid sit motus,\n[[2019.18]] nec intelligetur quid sit quies; sed etiam verbis usu receptis vim fecere, ut ne statuere\n[[2019.19]] viderentur motum terrae, itaque negaverunt terram moveri, quia scilicet cum coelo seu\n[[2019.20]] vortice suo deferatur, nec proinde ab ambientibus corporibus recedat, quod quanquam\n[[2019.21]] falsum sit (nam licet cum vortice suo moveretur, minus celeriter tamen moveretur, quam\n[[2019.22]] materia subtilis ipsius vorticis); tamen licet verum poneretur non ideo motui terrae\n[[2019.23]] obesset, quis enim neget trabes moveri quae a flumine deferuntur, moventur enim\n[[2019.24]] nonnunquam tanta vi ut etiam pontes convellant. Itaque nos illi motum tribuemus, quod\n[[2019.25]] vim agendi habet. Unde patet etiam falso illos dixisse, id quod reale et positivum in motu\n[[2019.26]] est, aeque utrique corporum contiguorum a se recedentium competere. Potest enim vis\n[[2019.27]] agendi esse in uno tantum, adeoque et causa <angle bracket>variati situs</angle bracket>. </p>\n",
  "number": "367₅.",
  "title": "De causa motus",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:367₅. De causa motus DE CAUSA MOTUS Punctum moveri dicitur quod distantiam ab aliis punctis mutat ob causam in ipso existentem. Duorum punctorum A et B motus communis est si quatenus ita moventur eandem distantiam servent; ut liquidum cum vase, etsi per accidens eveniat, ut partes liquidi ob vas non...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>